  "notes": "vasiṣṭa: read as aorist middle of √vas 'clothe' (he clothed himself), subject unnamed (the Soma, by the sense of 'milked him'); a vocative 'Vasiṣṭa' is possible but not preferred. gāḥ 'cows' and avibhiḥ 'sheep' are literal; the text does not say milk or woollen strainer. 'tsīm' = sīm with a euphonic t after the final n of adhukṣan. hotrāt ā: ablative with ā 'from'; hotrā = the Hotṛ's office/function; not expanded to 'cup'. prathamaḥ: 'first' taken as predicate of īśiṣe.",
